=== SURVEY ===
- Reviewed AnalyticsSummary type: totalDistanceKm, totalEnergyKwh, totalCost, avgEfficiencyWhKm, co2SavedKg, vehicleComparison[]
- Hook: useAnalyticsSummary() in @/api/hooks/useAnalytics → /analytics/fleet?days=30
- WidgetStatGrid: accepts StatGridItem[], compact, cols (2|3|4). Renders StatCard per item.
- WidgetShell: freshness props (updatedAt, isFetching, isStale, isError, onRefresh)
- WidgetBigNumber: value, unit, label, subtitle, badge, animated
- AnimatedNumber: value, suffix, className, decimals
- Sparkline: data (number[]), color, height, width — returns null for empty arrays
- useSettings: convertDistance (mi→user), distanceUnit, currencySymbol
- unit-conversion.instructions.md: data is in km, useSettings.convertDistance takes miles
- Data flow: totalDistanceKm → kmToMiles if user wants mi, else keep km
- avgEfficiencyWhKm → multiply by MI_TO_KM if user wants Wh/mi, else keep Wh/km

=== REASONING ===
- Compact (1×2): AnimatedNumber showing total distance with suffix distanceUnit
- Standard (2×2): 4 stat cards via WidgetStatGrid cols=2: distance, efficiency, energy, cost/dist
- Wide (4×2): WidgetStatGrid cols=4 + sparkline row (renders when API provides trend arrays)
- Unit conversion: API returns km-based data. Use kmToMiles() for mi users, keep raw for km.
- Efficiency: Wh/km × 1.60934 = Wh/mi
- Cost per distance: totalCost / displayDist
- Null safety: all fields ?? 0, hasData check gates content vs EmptyState
- Sparkline future-proofing: cast data to Record and check for optional trend arrays
- All strings i18n via useTranslation('dashboard')

